<title>USA: McDonnell Douglas off in sync with Boeing.</title>
<headline>McDonnell Douglas off in sync with Boeing.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of McDonnell Douglas Corp were off three points at 57-1/2 in sympathy with Boeing Co, which was down 5-3/4 to 96-1/4, analysts said.</p>
<p>McDonnell shares have been trading in sync with Boeing's stock since the two aircraft companies announced a proposed merger agreement.  </p>
<p>BT Securities analyst Wolfgang Demisch said McDonnell Douglas traded lower based on a ratio set in the merger agreement.</p>
<p>Boeing shares dropped after the aircraft company reported lower than expected earnings, he said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
